    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Caroline Menjivar has represented the 20th District since 2022. She is a Marine veteran, former EMT and social worker. She previously worked as the East Valley representative for the Los Angeles mayor’s office. She chairs a Senate budget subcommittee on health and human services.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Caroline Menjivar has represented the 20th District since 2022.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She is a Marine veteran, former EMT and social worker.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "She previously worked as the East Valley representative for the Los Angeles mayor’s office.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She chairs a Senate budget subcommittee on health and human services.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She authored a law requiring large employer health plans to cover infertility treatment, including IVF. She opposed Medi-Cal cuts for undocumented immigrants, saying people would lose coverage. She voted against a bill for denser housing near transit, arguing it would not serve working-class residents. Her office says in 2026 she secured $19 million for her district and had six bills signed into law, including paid postpartum leave for firefighters and hearing aid coverage for children.",
        "cites": [4, 5, 6],
